  "id": "manipuri_nata_sankirtana",
  "name": "Nata sankirtana (Manipuri ritual singing and drumming)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sankirtana is the ritual singing, drumming and dancing of the Vaishnava Meitei of the Manipur valley, performed in temples and domestic courtyards for religious festivals and life-cycle ceremonies. Typically two drummers playing the pung barrel drum (the khol card, in its Manipuri pung form with a wooden shell, stands in for it) and about ten singer-dancers with large cymbals (kartal) perform in a circle of seated devotees, a leader opening each song and the group responding. It is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage.",
  "recipe": "classic modern nata sankirtana, ritual Devotional, hindu branch. single leader group response. khol, large heavy loud clash manjira. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
